.TH "RAPTOR-COMPARE" 1 "2026-10" "RAPTOR Studio" "RAPTOR Studio Manual"
.SH NAME
raptor\-compare \- Run each MODEL with the same options and compare metric by metric.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBraptor compare\fR [\-h] [\-\-metric NAME] [\-f {text,json,csv}] [\-n N] [\-t T] [\-\-stop KIND[=VALUE]] [\-\-stats\-start T] [\-\-seed N] [\-j N] [\-\-timeout DURATION] [\-\-analysis LIST] [\-\-importance MODE] [\-\-weak\-type TYPE] [\-s PATH=VALUE] [\-\-set\-file FILE] [\-\-save\-model PATH] MODEL [MODEL ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run each MODEL with the same options and compare metric by metric.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Options
.TP
\fB\-\-metric\fR \fINAME\fR

.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI{text|json|csv}\fR

.SS Run control
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-runs\fR \fIN\fR
number of runs (default: the model's)
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-length\fR \fIT\fR
run length for a time\-terminated run
.TP
\fB\-\-stop\fR \fIKIND[=VALUE]\fR
time | failures=N | cycles=N (default: the model's)
.TP
\fB\-\-stats\-start\fR \fIT\fR
start statistics at T
.TP
\fB\-\-seed\fR \fIN\fR
salt every random stream (default: Raptor's fixed seed table)
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-jobs\fR \fIN\fR
parallel workers (default 1; N>1 is reproducible but not draw\-identical to 1)
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fIDURATION\fR
give up after DURATION, e.g. 90s, 10m (default 10m); partial results are kept
.TP
\fB\-\-analysis\fR \fILIST\fR
weak,cost,capacity (replaces the model's setting); 'none' clears all
.TP
\fB\-\-importance\fR \fIMODE\fR
IEC 61078 Annex D importance measures estimated by re\-simulation: improvement (RRW, Vesely\-Fussell), risk (RAW), both (adds Birnbaum). Costs one extra batch per block, two for 'both'
.TP
\fB\-\-weak\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR
weak\-link analysis type
.SS Changing parameters (a copy; the model file is untouched unless \-\-save\-model)
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-set\fR \fIPATH=VALUE\fR
change one field, repeatable; see 'raptor help set\-paths'
.TP
\fB\-\-set\-file\fR \fIFILE\fR
many PATH=VALUE lines (or a TOML/JSON table)
.TP
\fB\-\-save\-model\fR \fIPATH\fR
also write the changed model to PATH
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBraptor\fR(1)
